§ `Assertions`

-- d044: salary and super are wages (s 9AA(1)(a), s 9CB(1)).
#ASSERT `How much of this payment is wages` `d044: a month's salary to an employee` EQUALS 7000
#ASSERT `How much of this payment is wages` `d044: the employer's super contribution for that month` EQUALS 840
#ASSERT `How much of this payment is wages` `director's fees Jarrah pays Daniel` EQUALS 5000
-- A contractor outside the one prescribed class (reg 5) is paid no wages.
#ASSERT NOT `Is this payment wages` `an invoice from a freelance developer`
-- Reg 5 contract: the labour part, less the GST on it (s 9AA(1)(c), s 9HB(1)): 44,000 - 4,000.
#ASSERT `How much of this payment is wages` `a boat builder's labour contract, with GST` EQUALS 40000
-- Reg 6(a): a contract for a given result for a fixed fee is excluded.
#ASSERT `How much of this payment is wages` `a boat builder's fixed-fee contract for a given result` EQUALS 0
-- s 9BA(1); s 9HB(2): no GST reduction for a fringe benefit.
#ASSERT `How much of this payment is wages` `a car provided to an employee, taxable for FBT` EQUALS 3000
-- s 9BA(2).
#ASSERT `How much of this payment is wages` `an exempt benefit under the FBTA Act` EQUALS 0
-- s 9GA.
#ASSERT `How much of this payment is wages` `Jarrah as employment agent pays a placed worker` EQUALS 10000

#ASSERT `Are the wages taxable in WA` `work done wholly in Perth`
-- s 6A(1)(b)(i): based where the worker lives.
#ASSERT `Are the wages taxable in WA` `work across WA and NSW by a Perth resident`
#ASSERT NOT `Are the wages taxable in WA` `work across WA and NSW by a Sydney resident`
-- s 6A(1)(b)(ii): worker not based in Australia, employer based in WA.
#ASSERT `Are the wages taxable in WA` `work across WA and Singapore by a worker living abroad`
-- s 6A(1)(c).
#ASSERT `Are the wages taxable in WA` `work wholly in London paid into a Perth account`
-- d044: Jarrah's salary for work in Perth is WA taxable wages (s 5(2)).
#ASSERT `How much of this payment is WA taxable wages` `d044: a month's salary to an employee` `work done wholly in Perth` EQUALS 7000
-- s 5(2): exempt wages are not WA taxable wages.
#ASSERT `How much of this payment is WA taxable wages` `parental leave pay exempt under Part 5` `work done wholly in Perth` EQUALS 0

-- s 32(2): Daniel controls both (s 33(2) more than 50% of voting shares; s 33(5) sole owner).
#ASSERT `Am I grouped with the other business` `Jarrah and Daniel's consulting practice`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I grouped with the other business` `Jarrah and a company Daniel holds 40% of`
-- s 38(1): the Commissioner's exclusion, as an input.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I grouped with the other business` `Jarrah and the practice, excluded by the Commissioner`
-- s 38(2): related bodies corporate cannot be excluded.
#ASSERT `Am I grouped with the other business` `Jarrah and a related body corporate, excluded by notice`
-- s 31(1).
#ASSERT `Am I grouped with the other business` `Jarrah and a business its developer mainly works for`
-- s 33(3): more than 50%, so exactly 50% is not a controlling interest.
#ASSERT `Does the person hold a controlling interest` `60% of a partnership's profits`
#ASSERT NOT `Does the person hold a controlling interest` `exactly 50% of a partnership's capital and profits`
#ASSERT `Can I be made to pay the group's payroll tax` TRUE

#ASSERT `the annual threshold amount` EQUALS 1000000
-- Pay-roll Tax Act s 5(4): 5.5% from 1 July 2023; s 6 Table item 1 in the sliding scale period.
#ASSERT `What is my payroll tax rate` 2032 285600 1 EQUALS `5.5 per cent`
-- Sliding scale (Pay-roll Tax Act s 6(2), (3)): $200m for a whole 2021-22 year: (5.5m + 0.06 x 100m) / 200m x 100 = 5.75;
-- $3bn: (89.5m + 0.065 x 1.5bn) / 3bn x 100 = 6.2333...; to 4 places 6.2333.
#ASSERT `What is my payroll tax rate` 2022 200000000 1 EQUALS (`a sliding scale rate` 5.75)
#ASSERT `What is my payroll tax rate` 2022 3000000000 1 EQUALS (`a sliding scale rate` 6.2333)
-- An employer with $200m of WA wages in 2021-22 pays 5.75% on all of them: $11,500,000.
#ASSERT `How much payroll tax must I pay for the year` `$200 million of wages in 2021-22` EQUALS 11500000

-- d044: Jarrah's wages are under the $1,000,000 threshold, so no payroll tax yet (s 10(1)(a)).
#ASSERT `Which band am I in` `d044: Jarrah's first full year, 2031-32` EQUALS `nil: my wages are at or below the threshold`
#ASSERT NOT `Does my company pay payroll tax for the year` `d044: Jarrah's first full year, 2031-32`
-- d044: the part-year to 30 June 2031: threshold 1,000,000 x 30/365 = 82,191.78; wages 23,800 (s 10(3)(a)).
#ASSERT `How much payroll tax must I pay for the year` `d044: Jarrah's first month, June 2031` EQUALS 0
-- FORMULA (ss 8(4), 10(2)): TV = 1,000,000/6,500,000; deductable = 1,000,000 - 650,000 x TV = 900,000; tax 5.5% of 750,000.
#ASSERT `How much payroll tax must I pay for the year` `Jarrah grown to $1,650,000 of wages in 2034-35` EQUALS 41250
-- s 10(1)(b): at the upper threshold, tax on all wages.
#ASSERT `How much payroll tax must I pay for the year` `wages of exactly $7,500,000` EQUALS 412500
#ASSERT `How much payroll tax must I pay for the year` `wages of $8,000,000` EQUALS 440000
-- FORMULA (ss 11A, 10(4)): AAT = 1,000,000 x 73/365 = 200,000; deductable = 200,000 - 130,000 x TV = 180,000; tax 5.5% of 150,000.
#ASSERT `How much payroll tax must I pay for the year` `73 days as an employer with $330,000 of wages` EQUALS 8250
#ASSERT `Which band am I in` `a year before 2020-21` EQUALS `not encoded: this assessment year`

-- FORMULA (s 17(3A)): the group's deductable is its WA share of 900,000.
#ASSERT `How much payroll tax must my group pay for the year` `a group with $1,650,000 of wages, all in WA` EQUALS 41250
#ASSERT `How much payroll tax must my group pay for the year` `a group with $1,650,000 of wages, half in WA` EQUALS 20625
-- s 17(2)(b): Australian wages at or over the upper threshold, tax on all WA wages: 5.5% of 2,000,000.
#ASSERT `How much payroll tax must my group pay for the year` `a group with $8,000,000 of wages, $2,000,000 in WA` EQUALS 110000

-- d044: June 2031 wages of $23,800 do not exceed the $83,333 monthly threshold (s 24(1)(b)).
#ASSERT NOT `Must I apply to register for payroll tax` `d044: Jarrah in June 2031`
#ASSERT NOT `Must I lodge a monthly return` `d044: Jarrah in June 2031` FALSE
-- s 24(1)(b) counts interstate taxable wages too.
#ASSERT `Must I apply to register for payroll tax` `a nongroup month of $50,000 in WA and $40,000 interstate`
-- s 24(2): a group member must register for any WA taxable wages.
#ASSERT `Must I apply to register for payroll tax` `a group member's month of $5,000 in WA`
#ASSERT `How many days after the month do I have to lodge and pay` `d044: Jarrah in June 2031` EQUALS 21
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for not registering` EQUALS 20000
